Bootstrap: docker
From: pytorch/pytorch:2.1.2-cuda12.1-cudnn8-runtime

# LEAF + ViT/ConvNeXt image for HOPPER GPUs (H100, compute capability sm_90).
#
# Why this differs from leaf_vit.def (which targets an RTX 4070, sm_89):
#
#   TF 2.15 aborts on an H100 with
#       Check failed: err == cudaSuccess (98 vs. 0)   in GetGpuLaunchConfig
#   CUDA error 98 is cudaErrorInvalidDeviceFunction -- the kernels in those
#   wheels have no sm_90 code. TF 2.17 ships Hopper kernels.
#
#   TF 2.16+ switched to Keras 3, but leaf_audio subclasses tf.keras layers in
#   the Keras 2 style. Installing tf-keras restores that API; run_server.sh
#   detects the tf_keras package and exports TF_USE_LEGACY_KERAS=1 for you.
#
# TensorFlow is here only for Run6/Run7. Run5 and Run8 are pure PyTorch, so
# none of the sm_90/Keras trouble above applies to them -- on an H100, Run8 is
# the path of least resistance.
#
# Run8 adds ConvNeXt (MODEL=convnext), which imports timm. It needs two symbols
# that timm has moved and kept only as deprecated shims, so the build asserts
# them rather than letting a queued job discover it.
#
# Build in the portal:
#   Source          Singularity Definition File
#   Definition File this file
#   Name            leaf_vit_h100

%post
    set -e

    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libsndfile1
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # One pip command so the resolver sees every pin at once -- timm added in a
    # second command was free to drag numpy or torch with it.
    #
    # torchvision is pinned only because timm depends on it. The base image
    # already ships 0.16.2 (the release matching torch 2.1.2), so this is
    # normally a no-op; without it, pip is free to pick a torchvision whose own
    # torch requirement upgrades torch off the base image's CUDA build.
    pip install --no-cache-dir \
        "tensorflow[and-cuda]==2.17.1" \
        "tf-keras==2.17.0" \
        "gin-config" \
        "soundfile" \
        "einops" \
        "pandas" \
        "numpy==1.26.4" \
        "torchvision==0.16.2" \
        "timm==1.0.24"

    # Fail at build time rather than in a queued job. GPUs are not visible
    # during the build, so this checks imports and versions only -- the sm_90
    # kernels can only be proven by actually running on the H100.
    TF_USE_LEGACY_KERAS=1 python - <<'PY'
import os
os.environ.setdefault("TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL", "3")
import tensorflow as tf, torch, torchaudio, numpy, tf_keras, timm
print("tensorflow", tf.__version__)
print("tf_keras  ", tf_keras.__version__)
print("torch     ", torch.__version__)
print("torchaudio", torchaudio.__version__)
print("timm      ", timm.__version__)
print("numpy     ", numpy.__version__)
# With TF_USE_LEGACY_KERAS=1 this must resolve to the Keras 2 API that
# leaf_audio's layer subclasses expect.
_ = tf.keras.layers.Conv1D
assert tf.__version__.startswith("2.17"), "expected TF 2.17"
assert numpy.__version__.startswith("1."), "keep numpy < 2"
# torch comes from the base image. If pip has silently moved it, the CUDA
# build may no longer match the driver on the node -- catch that here.
assert torch.__version__.startswith("2.1.2"), "torch moved off the base image version"
# leaf_pytorch (Run5/Run8) imports torchaudio, and its C extension only loads
# against the exact torch it was built for.
assert torchaudio.__version__.startswith("2.1"), "torchaudio must match torch 2.1.x"
# The two timm symbols ConvNeXt/models/convnext.py imports. Both are deprecated
# shims in timm 1.x; if a future timm drops them, Run8 MODEL=convnext breaks
# and this is where it should surface.
from timm.models.layers import trunc_normal_, DropPath
from timm.models.registry import register_model
print("tf.keras OK, timm shims OK")
PY

%environment
    export TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=3
    # TF 2.17 is Keras 3 by default; leaf_audio needs the Keras 2 API.
    export TF_USE_LEGACY_KERAS=1

%labels
    Description LEAF (TensorFlow) + ViT/ConvNeXt (PyTorch), built for H100 / sm_90
    TensorFlow 2.17.1
    PyTorch 2.1.2+cu121
    timm 1.0.24
    Python 3.10

%help
    For Hopper GPUs. On sm_89 and older, leaf_vit.def (TF 2.15) is fine and
    matches the local Docker image.

    Run5/Run8 need only PyTorch; Run6/Run7 additionally need TensorFlow.
    Run8 with MODEL=convnext also needs timm and the ConvNeXt/ folder from the
    repo -- it is imported from the mounted project dir, not baked into the
    image, so nothing here needs rebuilding when that code changes.

    run_server.sh takes:  <dataset> <script> [VAR=VAL ...]

      singularity exec --nv -B /nfs-share-stgnode/home/<user> \
        --pwd /nfs-share-stgnode/home/<user>/Work \
        leaf_vit_h100.sif bash run/run_server.sh cremad Run8.py MODEL=convnext
